              },
        "strike_interpolator" : {
                "$ref" : "#/definitions/quantra_enums_Interpolator",
                "description" : "Deprecated for BlackVolSpec surfaces; retained for backward compatibility.\nMapping: (Linear,Linear)=>Bilinear, (LogCubic,LogCubic)=>Bicubic."
              },
        "ssvi_slices" : {
                "type" : "array", "items" : {"$ref" : "#/definitions/quantra_SsviSlice"},
                "description" : "eSSVI slices, strictly increasing expiry. Used only when base.shape=SsviParams.\nReference forward F_ref(T): if every slice carries `forward`, F_ref is built from them\n(implied dividend discount curve Dq(T_i) = F_i Dr(T_i) / S0, log-linear in discount, flat\nforward beyond the last slice); if none does, F_ref = S0 Dq(T) / Dr(T) from the spec spot,\ndividend and discount curves; a mix is rejected. For shape=SsviCalibrate F_ref comes from\nthe calibrated forwards in the same way; there the dividend curve is optional: with none,\nevery expiry needs call and put quotes at >= 2 common strikes (put-call-parity forward),\nelse the request is rejected."
